---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { vonar } from '../../data/vonar';

// Required by SignPath Foundation for its free code signing programme for open-source projects.
const workflowUrl = `${vonar.repoUrl}/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml`;
---

<Page
  title="Vonar code signing policy · Xami"
  description="How the Vonar installer is code signed: what is signed, who approves it, and what the plugin does with your data."
  eyebrow="Code signing policy"
  heading="Signed builds."
  headingMuted="From public code."
>
  <section class="card-block">
    <p><strong>Free code signing provided by SignPath.io, certificate by SignPath Foundation</strong></p>
    <p>Status: <strong>Application pending</strong>. Until it is approved, the installer is not signed yet.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2>What is signed</h2>
    <p>
      Only the Vonar installer (<code>Vonar-&lt;version&gt;-Setup.exe</code>). It is built by GitHub Actions from
      the public repository <a href={vonar.repoUrl}>itsXami/vonar</a>, using the build steps in{' '}
      <a href={workflowUrl}>.github/workflows/ci.yml</a>. Nothing built outside this pipeline is signed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2>Roles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Authors</strong> (write the code): Xami</li>
      <li><strong>Reviewers</strong> (review every change before it is merged): Xami</li>
      <li><strong>Approvers</strong> (approve each signing request by hand): Xami</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Vonar plugin and its installer do not send any data over the network. There is no telemetry, no update
      check and no account. See also the <a href="/legal/">privacy notice</a> for this website.
    </p>
  </section>
</Page>
